<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  WyyyschokkFangPendantFactions.xml        Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-09-17

  WYYYSCHOKK_FANG_PENDANT_1. RimStarWars: Trophy Craft
  (mandrake.rsw.trophycraft) ships the mechanism
  (RSW_TrophyCraft_ObserverBraveFang, a ThoughtWorker keyed off a
  DefModExtension's factionDefNames list) with that list EMPTY — it does not
  know the Utinni campaign's factions. This patch is the wiring: campaign
  data belongs in RimUtinni, never RimStarWars.

  Three defNames, verified against live sources, not guessed:
    - Wildsteam Clan  -> RUT_Jawa_WildsteamClan
      (src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/FactionDefs/JawaWildsteamClan.xml,
      an authored RUT_ def — <defName>RUT_Jawa_WildsteamClan</defName>.)
    - Blackstar Company -> Pirate
      (BlackstarCompany.xml patches vanilla `Pirate` in place — a reskin,
      never a new def; faction_roster_v2.md:409 confirms
      "Blackstar Company | vanilla `Pirate`".)
    - Deep Tribe -> TribeCivil
      (DeepDesertTribes.xml patches vanilla `TribeCivil` in place, relabelled
      "Deep Desert Tribes" — a reskin, never a new def.)

  Wrapped in PatchOperationConditional (test on the exact node being
  written) rather than a bare MayRequire'd Add: MayRequire alone guards only
  "is the mod present", not "does the xpath still resolve" if
  RSW_TrophyCraft_ObserverBraveFang or its modExtension is ever renamed. A
  patch that matches nothing logs nothing either way, so this degrades
  silently rather than red on any future rename.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.trophycraft">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThoughtDef[defName="RSW_TrophyCraft_ObserverBraveFang"]/modExtensions/li/factionDefNames</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThoughtDef[defName="RSW_TrophyCraft_ObserverBraveFang"]/modExtensions/li/factionDefNames</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_WildsteamClan</li>
        <li>Pirate</li>
        <li>TribeCivil</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
